                        "entry_id": "d0e95b96-e48b-3672-b705-8047ba9b4688",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relating to or denoting the group of Indo-European languages comprising Sanskrit and the modern Indian languages which are its descendants."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "267408e3-33f2-37cd-b722-bf8050cb46f9",
                        "entry_id": "d0e95b96-e48b-3672-b705-8047ba9b4688",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relating to the Brahmic scripts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50ff915e-1115-3a0e-8c0d-0e1ce63fbbab",
                        "entry_id": "d0e95b96-e48b-3672-b705-8047ba9b4688",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to India or its people, culture and languages; Indian."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6539cda8-43fe-4635-b49e-4b51d275a53c",
                                "sense_id": "50ff915e-1115-3a0e-8c0d-0e1ce63fbbab",
                                "text": "Clearly, men like ʿAin al-Mulk and Aravit Rama Raja could not have migrated successfully between the predominantly Islamicate world of Bijapur and Golconda and the more Indic world of Vijayanagara had they not been proficient in Telugu or Kannada as well as in Dakhni or Persian."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "721a2382-207c-495d-bf37-74c578128a66",
                                "sense_id": "50ff915e-1115-3a0e-8c0d-0e1ce63fbbab",
                                "text": "Quite different in style from the red stone torso, it also shows links to later Indic art (Fig. 2.5). Found at Mohenjo-Daro in one of the later strata, this small image is probably of a date late in the history of the site."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63711abb-b94b-4770-8f31-18ea10c541a4",
                                "sense_id": "50ff915e-1115-3a0e-8c0d-0e1ce63fbbab",
                                "text": "Indic philosophy, on the other hand, divides people into three groups, as it has two separate definitions for Dharma and religion."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
